      "lineNbr": 251,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-23T03:28:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is dependent on enabling `CHARGER_SM5803`, and it\u0027s particularly redundant to repeat the charger name after putting this all inside a `menuconfig` and the options in their own file; remove \"SM5803\" from this and all other options.\n\nWe can use a `range` here to limit the value to the supported range as well (but should also keep the clamping logic in the code, to protect against errors in the kconfig).\n\nThis also doesn\u0027t \"enable a driver\", it sets a value and the help should specify what the units are. Something like this seems much clearer to me:\n\n```suggestion\nchoice\n\tprompt \"IBAT prochot threshold (mA)\"\n\trange 0 37800\n\tdefault 37800\n\thelp\n\t  Set the current threshold in milliamps for IBAT to trigger\n\t  prochot. Value is rounded to the next lowest multiple of 600\n\t  mA.\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 247,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 251,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "ee2d240f5eaff054eb1918c0f71e604e8fee3a8d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
